1
00:00:00,009 --> 00:00:07,953
A loan file rarely fakes a whole document. It changes one number. Here the payslip says 86,500, but its own arithmetic and its own words say 68,500.

2
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:15,099
SAKSHI runs the ten stages from the brief. Each finding is weighed by how reliable its witness is, must survive its innocent explanations, and lands on one of three rungs.

3
00:00:15,099 --> 00:00:19,840
Five documents of one loan application: payslip, bank statement, application form, ID card, employment letter. Memory is cleared first.

4
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,583
The progress bar walks the ten stages of the brief, on this laptop, offline.

5
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:26,536
Potential manipulation, inconsistencies, observations. The processing time is the real, unedited run time.

6
00:00:29,606 --> 00:00:32,968
Type, confidence, cues, modality, witness level and SHA-256 for every file.

7
00:00:32,968 --> 00:00:39,024
Every field with its raw and normalised value, confidence, extraction method and location on the page; text painted over inside the payslip file is listed too.

8
00:00:39,024 --> 00:00:45,897
68,500.00 is still in the payslip file, under a filled shape, with 86,500.00 drawn on top.

9
00:00:45,897 --> 00:00:52,047
As submitted: 86,500. The smallest change that makes every rule hold: 68,500.

10
00:00:52,047 --> 00:00:58,742
Net pay reads 86,500, but gross minus deductions and the amount written in words are consistent only with 68,500.

11
00:00:58,742 --> 00:01:06,770
The claim graph links each document to what it states; red lines are conflicts, such as the bank’s salary credit against the payslip.

12
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:13,550
Seven findings on the statement and the application converge on one hidden loan: an EMI of 24,500 shown as 14,500.

13
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:20,254
A digit in 14,500.00 is a pixel copy of a digit in 1,180.00: two numbered boxes on the scanned statement.

14
00:01:20,254 --> 00:01:26,761
Not everything escalates: a date of birth one digit apart stays an INCONSISTENCY, because a typo is still a plausible explanation.

15
00:01:26,761 --> 00:01:33,531
MOHD ARIF KHAN versus Mohammed Arif Khan is only an OBSERVATION: transliteration explains it, and the table shows each innocent explanation and its test.

16
00:01:33,531 --> 00:01:37,062
Nine pixel sensors, with a noise map for every page.

17
00:01:37,062 --> 00:01:44,686
Every evidence item with its document, page and pixel box. Click a location and the original page opens with that region boxed.

18
00:01:44,686 --> 00:01:48,207
Summary, hypotheses, areas that need verification and the limitations of this investigation.

19
00:01:48,207 --> 00:01:53,381
Every step is logged with the hash of the step before it, so a later edit is detectable. Download it with the dossier as HTML and JSON.

20
00:01:53,381 --> 00:01:56,686
The same applicant’s genuine documents, plus one damaged PDF.

21
00:01:56,686 --> 00:01:58,833
Same ten stages, same thresholds.

22
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:06,570
The damaged file is rejected with a reason and the rest is analysed: no potential manipulation, no inconsistency.

23
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:08,701
Coverage map: every field marked strong, weak or blind.

24
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:12,598
A different applicant (red-team case RT7). SAKSHI remembers the cases it has already seen on this machine.

25
00:02:12,598 --> 00:02:13,832
Same ten stages, same thresholds.

26
00:02:13,832 --> 00:02:23,494
The ID photo and the salary account were already seen in an earlier case under a different name.

27
00:02:23,663 --> 00:02:29,109
A red-team attack: a scanned payslip edited in a PDF editor. The scan is untouched; a box hides the real figure and new text sits on top.

28
00:02:29,109 --> 00:02:33,034
Loaded from the console’s demo list.

29
00:02:33,034 --> 00:02:35,177
Same ten stages, same thresholds.

30
00:02:35,177 --> 00:02:40,398
Five potential-manipulation findings.

31
00:02:40,398 --> 00:02:45,562
What a reader sees: 88,500. The scan inside the same file, underneath: 68,500.

32
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:53,581
Every number comes from a test anyone can rerun, including where SAKSHI fails: on real receipts the middle tier cannot separate forged from genuine.

33
00:02:53,581 --> 00:02:58,107
SAKSHI. Evidence, not verdicts.
